From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <devnull@projectluma.local>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 19:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] window, header-bar: one title row per window

When a window's header bars live inside the panes of the split view that is
its work surface, the window itself provides the 42px title row (identity and
window controls, on the window material, above the islands). The pane header
bars take pane roles: the sidebar pane's header becomes a pane toolbar that
carries its actions on the command row and has no title row of its own; the
content pane's header stays a flat pane header with the page title and its
actions. Neither owns the identity or shows window controls. The roles lift
while a split view is collapsed. AdwApplicationWindow and AdwWindow own the
title row; adw-header-bar-private.h carries the toolkit-internal handoff.
---

